  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Jubilee South</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Jubilee South/Brazil is part of an international network present in over 30 countries aiming at strengthening democratic popular participation in the decision-making concerning the debt of Southern countries and publicizing the international mechanisms that keep poor countries in debt.

This project is part of the Economic Justice Programme, a partnership between CAFOD and 4 church-based organisations, whose goal is to achieve greater economic justice in Brazil by addressing the key development issues of debt, trade, governance and human rights with a focus on awareness-raising, participation, social mobilisation and advocacy.

The project is: (1) publicizing the Economic Justice Programme&apos;s theme &quot;debt, social rights and social security reform&#x201D; and monitoring the government&#x2019;s activities towards social inclusion; (2) increasing the participation of the 80 regional representatives in actions that encourage direct participation of the population in the defence of social rights and training them to engage in &#x201C;Citizen Audits&#x201D;; (3) advocating in favour of the unconditional defence of all the social rights established in the Constitution, currently threatened by the social security reform; (4) Monitoring the government&apos;s actions related to the payment of the public debt and advocating for more transparency in the government&#x2019;s accounts (5) strengthening the partnership between Jubilee Brazil and Jubilee South in other countries.</narrative>
  </description>
